          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "पैलां (pailā̃) is a tadbhava, a word inherited and reshaped by sound change. It comes from prathila, \"first\", a form CDIAL reconstructs from its descendants. CDIAL lists Old Marwari pahalo under it (CDIAL 8652). पैलां (pailā̃), \"before\", is a form of the word for \"first\", built on Sanskrit prathama, \"first\"."
            }
          ]
